--TEST--
`spawn script 'child.nvs'` runs the `child.nvs` beside the file that contains the spawn, whatever the working directory is, and a relative path built while the program runs throws a `RuntimeError` before any child starts — `rule:programs/relative-paths-resolve-from-their-file`
--FILE nvs.toml--
[capabilities.script]
spawn = true
--FILE child.nvs--
<?nvs
echo "the child beside case.nvs ran\n";
--FILE jobs/child.nvs--
<?nvs
echo "the child beside jobs/Runner.nvs ran\n";
--FILE jobs/Runner.nvs--
<?nvs
class Runner {
    public static function run(): void {
        // Written in `jobs/`, so the path written here names `jobs/child.nvs`. The case
        // runs from the folder above, where another `child.nvs` waits.
        var $done = await spawn script "child.nvs" with(output: "capture");
        echo $done->output;
    }
}
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:programs/file-paths-a-relative-path-starts-at-the-folder-of-its-file
require './jobs/Runner.nvs';

Runner::run();

// Written in this file, so the same written path names the `child.nvs` beside it.
var $here = await spawn script "child.nvs" with(output: "capture");
echo $here->output;

// A path built at run time is not joined to anything, and a relative one
// throws in the parent: no child starts, so there is no `ScriptResult`.
string $name = "child" . ".nvs";
try {
    spawn script $name;
    echo "unreachable\n";
} catch (RuntimeError $relative) {
    echo $relative->message, "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
the child beside jobs/Runner.nvs ran
the child beside case.nvs ran
`spawn script` needs an absolute path, and `child.nvs` is relative
help: build the path with `Core\Path::join` from a folder you know, or with `Core\Path::fromCwd` for a path typed on the command line
